      "pageDescription": "Listen to The Poynter Report Podcast on Spotify. You have questions about the media. We have answers. The Poynter Institute, the worldwide leader in supporting journalism, truth and democracy, opens the curtain for a deep look inside the media world. Join veteran journalist and media critic Tom Jones and his industry insider guests for 20 minutes every other week to feel informed and invested in the most relevant media news. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information.",
      "evidenceText": "The Poynter Report Podcast | Listen to the Podcast on Spotify The Poynter Report Podcast Tom Jones Follow You have questions about the media. We have answers. The Poynter Institute, the worldwide leader in supporting journalism, truth and democracy, opens the curtain for a deep look inside the media world. Join veteran journalist and media critic Tom Jones and his industry insider guests for 20 minutes every other week to feel informed and invested in the most relevant media news. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. 4.9 (24) News & Politics All Episodes 2026 Election Debrief with CNN's John King S7 E4: CNN's National Correspondent John King joins the podcast to talk about what he calls an \"historic epic reckoning\". The man who stands in front of the \"Magic Wall\" discusses what caused the Democratic \"blue tsunami\". King provides insight on races in Ohio, Michigan, North Carolina, Florida and more. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Monday 43 min Fact Checking the Midterm Elections S7 E3: Which candidates are telling the truth, and which ones aren't? PolitiFact Editor-in-Chief Katie Sanders joins the podcast with a look at key midterm Senate races. What are the top issues and what are the biggest lies? Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Oct 26 35 min Fox News Pentagon Correspondent Jennifer Griffin S7 E2: Longtime Fox News Pentagon Correspondent Jennifer Griffin joins the Poynter Report Podcast to discuss her nearly 30-year career with the network. She also provides frank opinions about restrictive Pentagon press policies and her former Fox colleague, and now Secretary of Defense, Pete Hegseth. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Oct 12 50 min Exclusive Interview with MS NOW's Rachel Maddow S7 E1: Season 7 begins with an exciting interview with MS NOW anchor Rachel Maddow. She joins Tom Jones on the Poynter Report to discuss all things President Trump including his recent White House media ban. Rachel also discusses her new documentary and book. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Sep 28 39 min An Exciting New Source for Health and Wellness Information In the season six finale of The Poynter Report, learn about an exciting new offering from the Poynter Institute. Well Informed is designed for consumers looking for accurate health and wellness information. From the people who bring you PolitiFact, find out how Well Informed will be an advocate for consumers. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Jul 20 24 min What is going on at CBS? Wall Street Journal Media Reporter Isabella Simonetti joins host Tom Jones to discuss the recent turmoil at CBS News. Get insight on the status of 60 Minutes. Also, learn what could be next for CNN. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Jun 29 24 min Covering the 2026 FIFA World Cup This is a must-listen to episode for anyone who enjoys soccer/football. The guest is Laura Williamson, Editor-in-Chief of UK and Europe at The Athletic. Hear about how one of the world’s leading sports news organizations is preparing for one of the biggest sporting events on the planet. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Jun 8 31 min A Seasoned Journalist Looks Back and Forward S6 E1: Season six kicks off with the former national media writer for the Associated Press, David Bauder. He joins The Poynter Report to reflect on his nearly 40-year career with the wire service. Among the topics: his interviews with members of the Beatles, the winners and losers in the media world, and press coverage of President Trump. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. May 18 36 min A Poynter Report Exclusive: When AI Crosses the Line in Journalism For the first time the Poynter Institute's Alex Mahadevan and Angela Fu discuss their investigation that uncovered a troubling case where Nota, an AI company, blurred the line between innovation and plagiarism. Their investigation not only led to the project’s shutdown but also sparked bigger questions about trust, ethics, and the future of news in an AI-driven world. Season 5 Episode 6. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Apr 16 32 min Reporting from Iran: Risks, Access, and the Realities of War Coverage The Poynter Report features an interview with Frederik Pleitgen, Senior Correspondent for CNN International, who discusses the challenges of reporting in Iran during an ongoing conflict. He describes the difficulty of gaining access to restricted areas, working under surveillance, and reporting amid constant airstrikes, all while having limited internet access. Pleitgen also reflects on the human impact of war, sharing how civilians cope with fear and uncertainty, and how covering these events leaves a lasting emotional impact on journalists. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Apr 1 29 min The Paramount Warner Bros. Discovery deal. What does it mean? The Poynter Report welcomes media reporter Sara Fischer to discuss the key ramifications of the mega deal. Drawing on her work at Axios, Fischer explains the corporate drama involving Warner Bros. Discovery, Netflix, and Paramount. She also addresses CNN's uncertain future. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Mar 18 30 min Reporting through a crisis in Minnesota The Poynter Report welcomes Steve Grove, CEO and Publisher of the Minnesota Star Tribune, to discuss how his journalists covered the protests in Minneapolis. He reflects on the emotional toll of reporting on deeply personal community stories, the arrests of local journalists, and the growing fight against misinformation. Grove also highlights the dangers reporters faced and the paper’s mission to strengthen trust, accountability, and unity through local journalism during a time of crisis. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Mar 4 35 min Load more episodes Home Search Your Library Premium ,",
