      "id": "faf5dcda7d45b9685c93737eb6101aa7ea043cdb7cbfb67235b1811544604dc1",
      "title": "Misread Mandate",
      "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgkjgmkn10ko",
      "category": "uncategorized",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T22:02:51.489Z",
      "httpStatus": 200,
      "finalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgkjgmkn10ko",
      "contentType": "text/html",
      "pageTitle": "Jake Paul, Zuckerberg and Musk: Who&#x27;s at Trump&#x27;s inauguration? - BBC News",
      "pageDescription": "The inauguration guestlist features unlikely names including MMA fighter Conor McGregor and influencer Jake Paul.",
      "evidenceText": "Jake Paul, Zuckerberg and Musk: Who's at Trump's inauguration? - BBC News Figure caption, Watch: Tech CEOs, celebs and presidents - see who’s at Trump's inauguration By Natasha Preskey BBC News Published 20 January 2025 A host of less familiar faces mingled with former presidents, family members and US officials at Donald Trump's inauguration. From tech billionaires to social media influencers, here's your guide to the guest list. Tech billionaires Trump's close and controversial friendship with X owner Elon Musk is well known but Musk wasn't the only tech chief at Monday's inauguration. Mark Zuckerberg, who earlier this month announced Meta was to get rid of factcheckers and \"dramatically reduce the amount of censorship\" on its platforms, was also there. Image source, Getty Images Image caption, Meta's Mark Zuckerberg and Lauren Sanchez, who is married to Amazon founder Jeff Bezos, in quiet conversation Image source, Getty Images Image caption, A place setting for Zuckerberg for a lunch in Statuary Hall Image source, Reuters Image caption, Elon Musk at the Rotunda TikTok CEO Shou Zi Chew also made an appearance. It comes as TikTok is resuming service in the US after Trump said he would issue an executive order to give the app a reprieve. Trump previously backed a ban on the platform but on Sunday promised to delay its implementation and allow more time for a deal to be reached with the app. Image source, Reuters Image caption, TikTok CEO Shou Zi Chew was pictured at the inauguration, with podcaster Joe Rogan visible in the foreground Image source, Reuters Image caption, Amazon founder Jeff Bezos and his wife Lauren Sanchez mingled with other tech billionaires Image source, EPA-EFE/REX/Shutterstock Image caption, Apple CEO Tim Cook was very close to the action as Donald Trump and his Vice President JD Vance were sworn in Influencers and celebrities Another tech billionaire in the audience was Sam Altman, CEO of OpenAI, who was pictured posing for a group selfie with boxer and influencer Jake Paul, and Paul's brother, wrestler and influencer Logan. Image source, Getty Images Image caption, Sam Altman grabs a selfie with Jake and Logan Paul Image source, Getty Images Image caption, The unlikely trio chatted animatedly ahead of the ceremony Logan and Jake Paul also shared a selfie of them travelling to the inauguration with controversial Irish MMA fighter Conor McGregor. McGregor has said he agreed to an exhibition boxing match against Logan Paul in India, however the bout is not confirmed. Last year McGregor lost a civil case where he was accused of raping Nikita Hand in a Dublin hotel in December 2018. Logan Paul has also recently faced fresh questions over his cryptocurrency dealings amid ongoing concerns he may have profited from misleading fans. Paul denied any wrongdoing. This X post cannot be displayed in your browser. Please enable Javascript or try a different browser. View original content on X The BBC is not responsible for the content of external sites. Skip X post by Jake Paul Allow X content? This article contains content provided by X. We ask for your permission before anything is loaded, as they may be using cookies and other technologies. You may want to read X’s cookie policy , external and privacy policy , external before accepting. To view this content choose ‘accept and continue’ . Accept and continue The BBC is not responsible for the content of external sites. End of X post by Jake Paul McGregor was also pictured alongside the head of the Reform UK political party, Nigel Farage, at a Trump rally on Sunday night. Image source, Reuters Image caption, Nigel Farage comes face-to-face with Irish MMA fighter Conor McGregor at Sunday's rally Media names Image source, EPA-EFE/REX/Shutterstock Image caption, Joe Rogan was at the inauguration with his wife Jessica Ditzel, who usually keeps a low profile Podcaster Joe Rogan was also seen in the inauguration crowd. In 2020, Rogan endorsed Democrat candidate Bernie Sanders but shortly before the 2024 election, he endorsed Trump . At times, Rogan's editorial approach has landed him in hot water - for example, during the Covid pandemic, when he was accused of spreading vaccine misinformation. In 2022, Rogan apologised after footage emerged of him repeatedly using the n-word in early episodes of his show. Image source, Getty Images Image caption, Rupert Murdoch with his wife Elena Zhukova Rupert Murdoch, chairman emeritus of News Corporation, which owns Fox News, the Wall Street Journal, the Sun and the Times, was pictured with his fifth wife Elena Zhukova. Mr Murdoch, 93, married the retired Russian biologist last year in a ceremony at his Californian vineyard. Former presidents All four of the living former presidents attended, as is customary. Much has been made in the media of Michelle Obama not accompanying her husband, Barack, who cut a solitary figure as he walked into the Rotunda. Obama lined up at the front of the stage alongside George W Bush and Bill Clinton. Image source, Getty Images Image caption, Former President Bill Clinton and Hillary Clinton, who lost out to Trump in the 2016 election, stand next to George W Bush, his wife Laura and Barack Obama Foreign dignitaries World leaders and politicians made the ceremony too. One familiar face was former British Prime Minister Boris Johnson. When Johnson came to power in 2019, Trump called him \"a good man\", adding: \"They call him Britain Trump.\" Image source, Getty Images Image caption, Boris Johnson arrives for the inauguration Others included Italy's far-right prime minister, Giorgia Meloni, Argentina's maverick libertarian president, Javier Milei, and China's vice president, Han Zheng. Image source, EPA-EFE/REX/Shutterstock Javier Milei has been described by both supporters and detractors as \"crazy\" and during his presidential campaign in 2023, he brandished a chainsaw to symbolise his determination to substantially cut public spending. He appeared to be a popular figure at the inauguration, posing for selfies with several US representatives. Image source, Reuters Image caption, US Representative Kat Cammack takes a picture with Argentina's president Image source, Reuters Image caption, Milei also posed with US representative Claudia Tenney The Trump family Trump's family packed on to the stage to gather around him as he was sworn in. Lined up behind Trump and his wife Melania were Barron, 18, Donald Junior, 47, Ivanka, 43 and Tiffany, 31, who was side on to the camera. Eric, 41, can be seen behind Ivanka. Image source, Getty Images Outgoing President Joe Biden watched Trump speak from the sidelines. In the background were Amazon founder Jeff Bezos (mostly hidden by JD Vance), Google CEO Sundar Pichai and Elon Musk. Image source, Reuters Here's a reminder of who's who in the Trump family: Notable absences Some notable figures decided to give the inauguration a miss. Barack Obama attended without his wife Michelle, who announced last week that she would not be there, despite attending Trump's first swearing-in in 2017. Her office did not provide an explanation. Also missing was Karen Pence, the wife of former Vice President Mike Pence, with whom Trump had a falling out over Pence's refusal to overturn the 2020 election results. Former House Speaker Nancy Pelosi, a long-time Democratic leader and Trump adversary, also did not attend, having recently undergone hip replacement surgery. Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, a leading figure in the Democratic Party's progressive wing, announced she would skip the inauguration in a widely-shared video on Instagram on Sunday. Who sat where? Sitting closest to Trump were former President Joe Biden and entrepreneur and former Republican presidential candidate Vivek Ramaswamy. Last year, Trump said he would create an advisory agency called the Department of Government Efficiency (Doge) , to be headed by Ramaswamy and Elon Musk. To Trump's left, close family members rubbed shoulders with Mark Zuckerberg, Jeff Bezos and Elon Musk. To Trump's right, media mogul Rupert Murdoch sat alongside world leaders including the Italian prime minister and the president of Argentina. The prominence of the world's most powerful businessmen may be setting the tone for Trump's second term. Last week, Democrat Senators Elizabeth Warren and Michael Bennett, shared a letter addressed to the tech executives, accusing them of trying to \"cozy up\" to Trump \"to avoid scrutiny, limit regulation and buy favor\". But for now, Trump appears to be enjoying being surrounded by the rich and the powerful. As he wrote on social media last month: \"Everybody wants to be my friend!!!\" Graphics by the Visual Journalism team and additional reporting by Laura Blasey LIVE: Follow BBC's live coverage IN PICTURES: Key moments of the inauguration WATCH: The new president's day so far EXPLAINED: What Donald Trump could do on day one FASHION: Melania's striking hat and other eye-catching looks Related topics United States Donald Trump US election 2024 The video playlist Watch our pick of standout clips from across the BBC Previous Next 0:33 Skims offers refunds after £110 advent calendar backlash. 00:00:33, play video Skims offers refunds after £110 advent calendar backlash 0:52 Why have at least 10 US Air Force planes suddenly left UK? 00:00:52, play video Why have at least 10 US Air Force planes suddenly left UK? 0:53 Man smashes Chinese government building with digger. 00:00:53, play video Man smashes Chinese government building with digger 1:25 My life as the UK's youngest lighthouse keeper. 00:01:25, play video My life as the UK's youngest lighthouse keeper 0:48 Stricter school phone ban rules for England revealed. 00:00:48, play video Stricter school phone ban rules for England revealed 1:16 Will smoky bacon crisps really be banned? 00:01:16, play video Will smoky bacon crisps really be banned? 2:02 How model agencies helped Epstein access victims. 00:02:02, play video How model agencies helped Epstein access victims 1:17 Russian newspaper forced to close after eviction. 00:01:17, play video Russian newspaper forced to close after eviction 0:20 Drone drops food to chimpanzee in reserve cut off by floods. 00:00:20, play video Drone drops food to chimpanzee in reserve cut off by floods 1:17 M John Harrison on his Booker Prize-winning novel. 00:01:17, play video M John Harrison on his Booker Prize-winning novel 1:23 Civil servant who secretly had five jobs guilty of fraud. 00:01:23, play video Civil servant who secretly had five jobs guilty of fraud 1:04 What happened in court as Russell Brand was sentenced. 00:01:04, play video What happened in court as Russell Brand was sentenced 1:07 Why more women are turning to rage rooms. 00:01:07, play video Why more women are turning to rage rooms 0:49 Could U16s soon be banned from Vinted and eBay in UK? 00:00:49, play video Could U16s soon be banned from Vinted and eBay in UK? 1:21 What we know about Nvidia CEO's affair with suspected Chinese spy. 00:01:21, play video What we know about Nvidia CEO's affair with suspected Chinese spy 1:43 The facial recognition technology stopping shoplifters. 00:01:43, play video The facial recognition technology stopping shoplifters 0:55 World on track for hottest year on record. 00:00:55, play video World on track for hottest year on record 0:53 Thick fog disrupts UK travel as another weather warning issued. 00:00:53, play video Thick fog disrupts UK travel as another weather warning issued 0:53 How do you show your partner that you love them? 00:00:53, play video How do you show your partner that you love them? Top stories US Army soldier suspected of spying for Russia arrested in UK Published 1 hour ago David Walliams accused of sexual misconduct after losing injunction bid Published 1 hour ago What we know about the allegations against David Walliams Published 2 hours ago More to explore Why does Australia want Brits to swap Sydney for the outback? I took Vinted to court to get my money back Kim Kardashian's Skims offers refunds for $148 advent calendar after backlash Divorced after five days: 'My sham husband made me believe he loved me' My life as the UK's youngest lighthouse keeper. Video My life as the UK's youngest lighthouse keeper Meet Stephanie Case - the first woman to run 100 miles in Antarctica 'Baffling but brilliant' post-apocalyptic novel The End of Everything wins Booker Prize Prince William wants more protection from harassment for service women News Daily: Our flagship daily newsletter delivered to your inbox first thing, with all the latest headlines Elsewhere on the BBC A familiar fixture in film that reflects British life Comedian Bob Mortimer chooses his Desert Island Discs Dashcam Justice: Small cameras, big consequences The first execution by lethal injection in the US Most read 1 David Walliams accused of sexual misconduct after losing injunction bid 2 US Army soldier suspected of spying for Russia arrested in UK 3 Meghan's father Thomas Markle detained for allegedly cutting off ankle monitor, officials say 4 Train attack driver's '10 seconds' to change line 5 Seven in hospital after car 'mounts pavement' in Glasgow 6 French wartime resistance heroine Solange Alexandre dies aged 104 7 Why does Australia want Brits to swap Sydney for the outback? 8 Inside devastated front-line city that Russia wants Ukraine to give up 9 More than 12 US military aircraft leave second UK base 10 Stevie Wonder leaves cafe staff £1,000 tip window.__INITIAL_DATA__=\"{\\\"data\\\":{\\\"global-navigation?country=us&language=en-GB&service=news\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"global-navigation\\\",\\\"props\\\":{\\\"country\\\":\\\"us\\\",\\\"language\\\":\\\"en-GB\\\",\\\"service\\\":\\\"news\\\"},\\\"data\\\":{\\\"accessibilityLinks\\\":[{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Skip to content\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"#main-heading\\\"},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Accessibility Help\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/accessibility/\\\"}],\\\"signInLabel